# Generator and map data

Changes here affect every generated map and every user, including users who
never enable competition. They are the highest-cost, highest-blast-radius
changes in the project.

## Exploration areas

- Exploration areas come from real closed administrative or place polygons,
  selected by a versioned country-specific configuration (`DECISIONS.md`
  SPD-006). One `admin_level` value is not semantically equivalent worldwide.
- Never synthesise a polygon around a `place=*` node (product spec §8.3 item 5).
- Never invent grid or arbitrary fallback areas (spec §8.6).
- Never treat an MWM country identifier as a neighbourhood.
- Where no suitable subdivision or place polygon exists, the containing city,
  town, or village becomes the area. Outside any settlement there is no area,
  and personal exploration still works (SPD-007).
- Assignment must be deterministic for a fixed map-data version and policy
  version: highest-priority configured level first, then smallest containing
  polygon, then a stable identifier such as the OSM relation id (spec §8.8).

## Current baseline

Verify before relying on this; it was true on 2026-07-25.

- `data/mapcss-mapping.csv` retains only `boundary|administrative|2`, `|3`, and
  `|4`. Levels `|7`, `|9`, `|10`, `|11` are deprecated. Levels 5, 6, and 8 have
  no `boundary|administrative` entry at all.
- City boundaries are stored at runtime as an approximation — the intersection of
  a bounding box, a calipers box, and a diamond box — not as true polygons.
- `place|suburb`, `place|quarter`, and `place|neighbourhood` exist as searchable
  place types, not as exploration polygons.

## Route eligibility

- Eligibility rules follow product spec §13 and must be maintained as a
  versioned map-data policy accompanying the implementation (§13.4).
- Prefer client-side filtering over generator changes where both are possible.
  Generator changes raise maintenance cost and divergence from upstream.
- Sampling and derivation must be deterministic for the same source data and
  configuration (§14.3).

## Discipline

- Regenerated or auto-generated data files go in a separate commit from the
  source change that produced them (`docs/PR_GUIDE.md`). Use a matching prefix,
  e.g. `[styles] Regenerate …` or `[mapgen] …`.
- Any size impact on generated packages must be measured and reported, not
  estimated.
- Changing the HEALPix `nside` redefines every pixel identifier and invalidates
  every stored file on every device. Treat it as a breaking change requiring a
  decision entry.
